  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nThe array can be modified by performing the following operation on it:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N).\nThen, for each index jjj (1≤j≤N1 \\le j \\le N1≤j≤N),\n\nIf j&lt;ij \\lt ij&lt;i, add AiA_iAi​ to AjA_jAj​.\nIf j≥ij \\ge ij≥i, subtract AiA_iAi​ from AjA_jAj​ instead.\n\n\nNote that every element of AAA must be modified - you cannot leave elements unchanged.\n\nFor example, if A=[2,4,−1,3]A = [2, 4, -1, 3]A=[2,4,−1,3] and we choose i=2i = 2i=2, the array becomes [6,0,−5,−1][6, 0, -5, -1][6,0,−5,−1] because A2=4A_2 = 4A2​=4 so we add 444 to A1A_1A1​ and subtract 444 from A2,A3,A4A_2, A_3, A_4A2​,A3​,A4​.\n\nYou would like to make all the elements of AAA equal by performing the given operation several times (possibly, zero times).\n\nIs it possible to achieve this goal?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer: YES\\texttt{YES}YES if it's possible to make all the elements of AAA equal after performing several operations, and NO\\texttt{NO}NO otherwise.\n\n\nEach character of the output may be printed in any case: for example, the strings NO,no,No\\texttt{NO}, \\texttt{no}, \\texttt{No}NO,no,No and nO\\texttt{nO}nO will all be treated as equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100",
      "−1000≤Ai≤1000-1000 \\le A_i \\le 1000−1000≤Ai​≤1000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n1 -1\n3\n1 -3 2\n4\n5 5 5 5",
        "output": "Yes\nNo\nYes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: We can choose i=2i = 2i=2, and the operation affects the array as follows:\n\nA2=−1A_2 = -1A2​=−1.\nSo, we add −1-1−1 to A1A_1A1​ and subtract −1-1−1 from A2A_2A2​.\nThe array becomes [0,0][0, 0][0,0], all its elements are now equal.\n\nTest case 222: It can be shown that no sequence of operations can make all the elements become equal.\nTest case 333: All the elements are already equal."
      }
    ]
